# Merge only into main

Merging a pull request updates its base branch. If that base is not `main`,
the commits never reach `main`. #1750 was merged into
`cursor/landing-roadmap-proof-links` after that branch's own PR (#1745) had
already merged, so the work missed `main`.

## Before every `gh pr merge`

```bash
gh pr view <number> --json baseRefName,state,url
```

Merge only when `baseRefName` is `main` and `state` is `OPEN`.

If `baseRefName` is anything else:

1. Stop. Do not merge.
2. Retarget with `gh pr edit <number> --base main`, or branch from
   `origin/main` and open a new pull request.
3. Read the diff against `origin/main` first. Retarget only when that diff
   is the change you mean to land.

## Never

- Choose the base from the current checkout, the head branch, or a parent
  feature branch.
- Merge into `cursor/*`, `feat/*`, `fix/*`, or any branch other than `main`.
- Treat an open parent pull request as permission to merge into that parent.

"Merge the PR" means merge into `main`. Use another base only when the user
names that branch in the same request.
